    "report": "The notice of a new message now carries `listingId`, and the work is committed as `dafe44d` on `main`. I did not push, and I did not start a server.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Messaging:** `MessageSentEvent` and the shared `MessageSentPayload` now include the conversation's `listingId`. The event is built from the conversation's existing listing id, and `MessageSentHandler` passes it on.\n- **Notifications:** `listingId` flows from the integration event into the owing rule and onto the message notice body. Delivery sends the body unchanged, so the service receives `listingId` with `id`, `kind`, `accountId`, `conversationId` and `lang`.\n- **Storage:** the `notices` table already had a `listing_id` column from calendar-conflict notices, so no migration was needed. Message notices now write to it and read it back.\n- **Specs:** I updated the existing expectations for the new field.\n\n**Verification**\n- Typecheck passes, and eslint passes on the changed files.\n- Unit tests for Notifications and Messaging: 15 suites, 72 tests, all passing.\n- Full e2e suite: 114 suites, 607 tests, all passing. My filter also matched the whole e2e set, so this is more than the two specs I was aiming at.\n\n**Decisions and things to check**\n- **Branch:** you asked for the current branch, which is `main`. The repo guidance says to branch first when on the default branch. I followed your instruction. If you want a branch, it is one command away.\n- **Notices owed before this deploy:** message notices that exist but are not yet accepted have no `listing_id`. They will be sent with `listingId: null` at runtime, even though the type says `string`. I did not recover the listing from Messaging's data, because that would cross a context boundary. If you want these to carry a real id, that needs a backfill or a rule you choose.\n- **ADR and docs:** I did not update ADR 0057 or the other docs. The code comments were updated.\n- **Scope:** only the notice of a new message changed. Other notice kinds and the notice schema are untouched.",
